3. Answer B, compile error

Both enums have Active = "ACTIVE", so I thought passing one for the other would be fine. That is option A and it feels right, but it is wrong.

Enums do not work that way. Each enum is its own separate type, even when the values inside are exactly the same. So Status.Active and Level.Active are two different types to TypeScript, even though both are "ACTIVE". That is why passing Level.Active to a function that wants a Status gives an error.

